{:db/id "9e0f85f1-ff39-5312-bff8-33d9ab8cc369"
  :question/id #uuid "9e0f85f1-ff39-5312-bff8-33d9ab8cc369"
  :question/problem "Source question: Canvas Question 12, ID 59548397; submitted attempt 1.\n\nConsider the matrix $\\left[\\begin{array}{rrrr|r}1&0&0&3&0\\\\0&1&0&4&0\\\\0&0&1&2&0\\\\0&0&0&0&1\\end{array}\\right]$. Which of the following is correct?"
  :question/answer-fields ["f799d34a-9ddf-5c76-809e-e77ca6ee874b"]
  :question/worked-solution "It is in reduced row echelon form. The leading ones are in columns $1,2,3,5$, and each is the only nonzero entry in its column. The last row represents an inconsistent equation, but inconsistency does not prevent an augmented matrix from being in RREF.\n\nHistorical Canvas result: 0/2 points, submitted 2026-10-16 at 22:45 PDT."
  :db/ensure :question/validate}
{:db/id "2c578cff-dc02-5a8c-a845-b17dc50cfdc0"
  :assigned-problem/id #uuid "2c578cff-dc02-5a8c-a845-b17dc50cfdc0"
  :assigned-problem/content "9e0f85f1-ff39-5312-bff8-33d9ab8cc369"
