{:db/id "5ad511d8-4b57-57f2-ae47-a50a22ea161a"
  :question/id #uuid "5ad511d8-4b57-57f2-ae47-a50a22ea161a"
  :question/problem "Source question: Canvas Question 13, ID 59548427; submitted attempt 1.\n\nList the necessary elementary row operations to put the matrix $\\left[\\begin{array}{rrrr|r}1&2&1&5&2\\\\2&5&0&4&0\\\\1&2&1&3&1\\end{array}\\right]$ into a row echelon form.\n\nRemember that one of the conditions that a matrix needs to satisfy to be in reduced row echelon form is that the leading entry in each row is 1."
  :question/answer-fields ["cba5d5cc-93e6-53ca-ba04-9dbf7bc3a1bf"]
  :question/worked-solution "Give the operations as well as a resulting echelon matrix. The source requests row echelon form; the reminder separately states a condition for reduced row echelon form.\n\nHistorical Canvas result: 9/9 points, submitted 2026-10-16 at 22:45 PDT."
  :db/ensure :question/validate}
