  :question/problem "Source question: Canvas Question 2, ID 59595307; submitted attempt 1.\n\nSuppose $A$ is a $3\\times5$ matrix. Choose the matrix $M$ such that the product $MA$ is the result of applying the follow two elementary row operations in the order listed:\n\n1. Replace row 2 with 3 times row 1 added to row 2.\n2. Swap row 1 and row 3."
